{"results":[{"url":"https://katu.com/news/local/man-arrested-on-arson-charge-after-lighting-leaf-pile-on-fire-in-oregon-city","final_url":"https://katu.com/news/local/man-arrested-on-arson-charge-after-lighting-leaf-pile-on-fire-in-oregon-city","title":"Man arrested on arson charge after lighting leaf pile on fire in Oregon City","description":"Oregon City Police arrested a man Friday afternoon after they say he lit a pile of leaves on fire near the Clackamas County Community Solutions building. Police said they responded to the incident after a Clackamas County Probation officer saw smoke coming from near the steps to the Community Solutions building and saw the suspect, 53-year-old Sammy Piatt, standing near the fire. A probation officer detained Piatt and another officer used a fire extinguisher to put out the fire.","language":"en","text":"# Man arrested on arson charge after lighting leaf pile on fire in Oregon City\n\n---\n\nby KATU Staff\n\nSat, September 12, 2020 at 11:05 PM\n\nSammy Piatt booking photo courtesy Clackamas County Jail\n\nOREGON CITY, Ore. — Oregon City Police arrested a man Friday afternoon after they say he lit a pile of leaves on fire near the Clackamas County Community Solutions building.\n\nPolice said they responded to the incident after a Clackamas County Probation officer saw smoke coming from near the steps to the Community Solutions building and saw the suspect, 53-year-old Sammy Piatt, standing near the fire.\n\nA probation officer detained Piatt and another officer used a fire extinguisher to put out the fire.\n\nPolice said the fire was about 10 feet from the building.\n\nPiatt admitted he lit the leaves on fire. He was arrested on charges of second-degree arson and on a probation violation. He was lodged at the Clackamas County Jail.\n\nPolice ask the public to call 911 or the non-emergency number if they see any suspicious activity.","author":"KATU Staff","published_date":"2020-09-13T06:05:39.000Z","latency_ms":186.5854509815108,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}